; A query's head may find its open rows' posting empty and the slot it
; probed may then be taken by another head's open rows.  Each space
; below keys its third column; after the first query reads the head A,
; rows of eleven other heads open at the column are added, then a row of
; A open there, which the second query of A must meet.
